<section class="section section--raised reveal" aria-labelledby="path-h">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">From first call to won job</p>
      <h2 id="path-h">Four steps, one record.</h2>
      <p>The same enquiry record is used by sales, the site engineer and the project team. Nothing is re-entered when it moves on.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <div class="flow__item">
        <h3>Capture</h3>
        <p>Record the customer, city, monthly electricity bill, roof area and type, property type and whether the job is on-grid, off-grid, hybrid or micro-inverter. Note if subsidy or a bank loan is needed.</p>
        <div class="flow__path"><span>Enquiry</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Roof and bill</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Project type</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow__item">
        <h3>Qualify and follow up</h3>
        <p>Move the enquiry through solar-specific statuses, set priority, and schedule the next follow-up. Every call and note stays on the record.</p>
        <div class="flow__path"><span>Contacted</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Survey</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Proposal</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow__item">
        <h3>Survey and quote</h3>
        <p>Assign a site engineer from the enquiry. The survey and the priced quotation attach to the same record.</p>
        <div class="flow__path"><span>Enquiry</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Survey</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Quotation</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow__item">
        <h3>Convert</h3>
        <p>When the customer commits, the enquiry converts to a customer and a project. Calls, notes, documents and the survey carry across.</p>
        <div class="flow__path"><span>Won</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Customer</span><i>&rarr;</i><span>Project</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section reveal" id="features" aria-labelledby="feat-h">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
      <h2 id="feat-h">Built for how solar enquiries are actually worked.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="roles">
      <div class="role"><h3>A pipeline made for solar</h3><p>Eighteen built-in statuses cover the real journey, from contacted and site survey to feasibility, proposal, committed and won, plus cold, on hold, not feasible and existing solar.</p><ul><li>Priority and lead score</li><li>Residential and commercial types</li></ul></div>
      <div class="role"><h3>Duplicate protection</h3><p>Phone numbers are normalised and matched on entry and on import. A user with permission can override a match, and the reason is saved on the enquiry.</p><ul><li>Alternate phone numbers</li><li>Override reason recorded</li></ul></div>
      <div class="role"><h3>Bulk import with preview</h3><p>Upload a sheet from a campaign, an expo or a partner. Review every row before saving, then group the result as a list by source.</p><ul><li>Ready, invalid and duplicate rows flagged</li><li>Lists by source and default manager</li></ul></div>
      <div class="role"><h3>Assignment and collaboration</h3><p>Give each enquiry an owner, a manager and a site engineer. Add colleagues as collaborators with view, work or manage access.</p><ul><li>Bulk assignment</li><li>Managed by a person or a role</li></ul></div>
      <div class="role"><h3>Call and WhatsApp logging</h3><p>Call or message from a shared phonebook and record the outcome. The log keeps the status before and after, and the next follow-up date.</p><ul><li>Connected, busy, wrong number, call back later</li><li>Recordings attached to the enquiry</li></ul></div>
      <div class="role"><h3>Internal follow-up requests</h3><p>Ask a colleague to act on an enquiry with a reason, a priority and a note. They respond on the same record, so nothing is lost in chat.</p><ul><li>Request, response and clarification</li><li>Notes, email and meeting history</li></ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--raised reveal" aria-labelledby="imp-h">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Clean data from day one</p>
      <h2 id="imp-h">Import a whole campaign without importing the duplicates.</h2>
      <p>Expo sheets, campaign lists and partner files arrive messy. HelioLattice shows what will happen to each row before anything is saved, so your pipeline stays clean and your team does not call the same customer twice.</p>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li>Preview every row before the import runs</li>
        <li>Duplicates inside the file and against existing enquiries are flagged</li>
        <li>Each import becomes a list tagged by source</li>
        <li>A default manager can be set for the whole list</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split__visual">
      <div class="ledger" role="group" aria-label="Example import preview">
        <div class="ledger__head">Import preview &middot; expo list</div>
        <div class="ledger__row"><span><b>Ready to import</b><small>New phone numbers, complete details</small></span><span class="pill">Ready</span></div>
